{"entryId":"3432","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3432:1","sourceSha256":"ca2581c7da6fd38357c501d55b3c94d034165f07ed438fb74aff1b6af0678a44","englishSha256":"eda4097d4f3426f5bfb6d0e011dedf0ddca64b1cbfcf4dbeb889311c4a88024e","citations":[{"id":"3432:1:link-003","he":[118,131],"en":[213,236],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_6.1"},"reference":"Tractate Derekh Eretz Rabbah 6:1","assessment":"The direct text has Anṭipaṭras, the vows and flogging, the sages’ discussion and Yehoshua’s visit. The parallel in Maḥzor Vitry preserves an alternate spelling and language about false vows.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tractate Derekh Eretz Rabbah 6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_6.1"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Machzor Vitry, Tractate Derekh Eretz 531:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Machzor_Vitry%2C_Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_531.5"},"witness":"Machzor Vitry, Berlin, 1893-97"}]},{"id":"3432:1:link-004","he":[48,75],"en":[66,115],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_6.1"},"reference":"Tractate Derekh Eretz Rabbah 6:1","assessment":"The entry names Yohanan ben Zakkai as the sender. The full tractate places the matter before him and the sages, and gives Yehoshua’s offer to go.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tractate Derekh Eretz Rabbah 6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_6.1"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."}]}],"inlineHebrew":[1,0],"holds":[],"notes":[],"comparisonEvidence":[]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
